CORE
main.c
--no-malloc-may-fail
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ length of the copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\[.*\.unwind\.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
^warning: ignoring
--
Without the malloc failure path, symbolic execution resolves every byte and
the loops end without --unwind; see test.desc, which needs --unwind 17 when
malloc may fail.
